    "chunk_size_bytes": 511,
    "chunk_text": "\"How can the government expect farmers to sell paddy at Rs. 120 per kilogram when it costs around Rs. 137 to produce it? If the government is concerned about consumers, it should focus on reducing production costs instead. A Rs. 20 increase in the paddy price will not significantly increase the price of rice,\" Tennakoon said.\n\nTennakoon said the National Agrarians' Unity would launch strong trade union action by mobilising the farming community if the government fails to revise the guaranteed paddy prices."
