    "language": "en",
    "md5": "3f478128e672ace58b169096d201b994",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 841,
    "chunk_text": "As part of the recovery programme, damaged national and rural roads will be repaired and reconstructed with improved drainage systems, slope stabilisation measures and strengthened road structures to make them more resilient to future extreme weather events.\n\nSupport will also be extended to cyclone-affected smallholder paddy farmers through livelihood assistance to help them restart agricultural production. Families whose homes were severely damaged or destroyed will receive owner-driven housing grants, released in stages based on verified construction progress.\n\nAccording to the ADB, the project will be implemented through government agencies responsible for transport, irrigation, agriculture and disaster recovery, with support from project implementation consultants and regular ADB review missions to ensure effective delivery."
  },
